# 03 — Root-Cause Fix, Escalation, Report & Review

<!-- GEN: Why: a root-cause fix at the owning layer with a regression test stays fixed, while environment triage and the 3-attempt time-box prevent destructive workarounds. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

Rules **D6**, **D7**, **D8**, **D9**, **D10**, **D11**, **D12**, and **D14**.

---

## 1. Root-Cause Fix & Red-to-Green Regression Prevention (`D7`, `D8`, `D9`)

1. **Regression Test First (`D8`, `{{unit_testing_link}}`):** Convert the minimal reproduction into a unit/integration test at the owning seam. Run it **red** and confirm it fails for the exact reported reason.
2. **Smallest Fix at the Owning Layer (`D7`, `{{clean_architecture_link}}`):** Fix the defect at the layer that owns the rule inside the task's approved **Scope / Files**. Check for sibling occurrences in the diff (`D6`). Do not bundle unrelated refactoring.
3. **Prove Red → Green → Undo-Red → Green:** Run the regression test (`PASS`), temporarily undo only the production fix to verify the test fails (`FAIL`), restore the fix, and re-run (`PASS`).
4. **Full Verification & Cleanup (`D11`):** Run the original reproduction, the module test suite, static checks (`{{verify_suite_cmd}}`), and the debug-tag sweep (`{{debug_cleanup_cmd}}`).

### Never Green-Wash (`D9` — Automatic `BLOCKER`)

| Forbidden Shortcut | Why It Is Forbidden |
|---|---|
| Editing, deleting, skipping, or weakening a test/assertion to make it pass | Hides the defect and destroys the guard that caught it |
| Broad catch blocks (`catch (_) {}`, `except Exception: pass`) or silent default returns (`null`, `[]`) | Turns a reproducible failure into silent state corruption |
| Hardcoded fallback/mock data in production code | Fabricates success while the underlying path remains broken |
| Loosening static types, adding cast/lint/type-checker suppressions | Disables compile-time safety across the module |
| Adding arbitrary sleeps, delays, or blind retries to mask race conditions or timeouts | Leaves the race or bottleneck in production |

