## 3. Hand-Off Debug Report Format (`D14`)

Include this block in the hand-off (or `FIXED` finding response) with redacted outputs (`<REDACTED>`):

```text
Symptom:      <what failed and where; reported by task check / reviewer / bug-hunt / tester / user>
Triage:       CODE_WRONG (task <id>, Expected: <...>)
Reproduction: <reproduce_cmd> @ <revision> -> exit 1 (<key failure output>)
Root cause:   <exact defect at path:line and why it occurred>
Fix:          <what changed at which owning layer and why>
Regression:   <test path::test_name> -> FAIL (exit 1) without fix, PASS (exit 0) with fix
Evidence:     <rows per evidence-standard: regression, suite, linter, type checker>
Ruled out:    H2 (<why>), H3 (<why>)
Debug tags:   <debug_cleanup_cmd> -> 0 matches / clean (PASS)
```

---

## 4. Review Severity (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`)

Code Reviewers grade debugging fixes on the unified 3-tier scale (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md` §2):

| Severity | Finding | Review Verdict Impact |
|---|---|---|
| `BLOCKER` | Any green-washing (`D9`); missing Red-to-Green regression test (`D8`) where a seam exists; leftover `[DEBUG-xxxx]`, debug print, or breakpoint (`D11`); unapproved contract/schema/dependency change (`D12`); any check `FAIL`s | `CHANGES_REQUESTED` (blocks approval) |
| `MAJOR` | Symptom patched in the caller/UI instead of the owning root-cause layer (`D6`, `D7`); sibling bug in the same diff left unfixed (`D6`); missing or incomplete Debug Report block (`D14`) | Must be fixed in the same phase scope |
| `MINOR` | Minor regression test naming or report formatting improvement | Optional (never blocks approval) |

